    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b769c1fa_89971d77",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/include/core-impl/StreamRemoteSubmix.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 71,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T18:05:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that since we always have the reader and the writer on different threads, we only need to make thread-safe the retrieval of the pointer itself. Thus, in the spirit of the proposal above, we should just have methods like these:\n\n```\nsp\u003cMonoPipe\u003e getSink() { std::lock_guard guard(lock); return sink; }\nsp\u003cMonoPipeReader\u003e getSource() { std::lock_guard guard(lock); return source; }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "10f4d3c17c9c94d5bd9cb432b642c5c4dfc78793",
