      "lineNbr": 120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T18:05:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since each `SubmixRoute` also contains a lock, we need to specify in a comment what is their relation: either they must never be held together, or they must always be acquired in a specific order. Looking at `DriverRemoteSubmix::init()` it seems that it\u0027s the latter case, and the vector lock must be taken first. However, that means we must do that in all cases in order to avoid deadlocks. Thus, it will actually be easier to require and ensure that these locks are never taken together.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 120,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 120,
        "endChar": 97
      },
      "revId": "10f4d3c17c9c94d5bd9cb432b642c5c4dfc78793",
